gamescope: GBM-allocated scanout buffers on the DRM backend (upstream issue #2309)

Why. On the NVIDIA proprietary driver (seen on 575 through 610) gamescope's DRM
backend scans out a corrupt band along the bottom of the screen at every
3840x2160 mode; 1080p and 1440p are clean, and other compositors on identical
DRM state are clean. The one difference is the scanout object: gamescope
allocates its output images with Vulkan (32 MiB at 4K), the clean compositors
allocate them with GBM (33,423,360 bytes, pitch x 2176) and import them, as
KWin does. Upstream report: https://github.com/ValveSoftware/gamescope/issues/2309

What. Adds IBackendScanoutBuffer + scanout-allocation hooks to the backend
interface; the DRM backend allocates its scanout buffers with GBM
(gbm_bo_create_with_modifiers2, a dup of the KMS fd) and rendervulkan imports
them as the composite output images. Off by default, behind the ConVar
drm_gbm_scanout (environment: gamescope_drm_gbm_scanout=1, which needs
gamescope-convar-env-override.patch on this 3.16.23 base). Optional libgbm
dependency: without it HAVE_GBM=0 and the path compiles out. The only side
effect seen is a failed GBM allocation for the 48x48 cursor, which gamescope
falls back from.

Source. NightHammer1000's branch poc/gamescope-gbm-route
(https://github.com/NightHammer1000/gamescope, head 2bfc18c, on 3.16.25):
the seven commits 6d46d29 a86849b ebbaf8b b384ac4 6605942 092a2e7 2bfc18c,
squashed. Rebased onto 3.16.23 after gamescope-nested-pointer-warp.patch and
gamescope-convar-env-override.patch: the code applied without conflicts; the
README build-dependency hunk and the subprojects/.gitignore commit were
dropped. Apply this patch AFTER those two, on stock 3.16.23 sources: it was
first rebased on a since-retired display-mode forwarding patch, and re-diffed
once that was gone (the src/meson.build hunks anchor on stock lines; no code
changed).

Quasar use: images/quasar-steam/quasar-steam sets the ConVar, with forced
composition, only for a direct-display session on nvidia-drm (quasar#453,
quasar#457). The source branch, built with this image's recipe, was clean on
the console host (RTX 5090, 610.57) at 3840x2160@60 and @240 for several
minutes of UI motion; this rebase is checked the same way before it ships.

